  "method": "Independently authored scalar kernels; optional deref, vector_slot, vector_read_index, vector_read_candidate, result_return and byte-loop pairs each compare the same algorithm with C. Vector_read_candidate uses the compiler-private authenticated SDK and source/Flow/MIR proof lane, not stable source admission. Byte_view and byte_index share one independent C loop and differ only in the Fairy inner-loop spelling; vector_read_index and vector_read_candidate likewise share one independent C workload. Same stdin input and QPC/output support. All workloads guard seed<65521 and rounds<=50000000; arithmetic is proven in-range over admitted inputs. Fairy retains ordinary checked arithmetic and full required product support; C does not link Fairy support. 5 alternating paired samples after one build/run warmup per workload/lane. Kernel time excludes input parsing, process startup and printing; result is consumed and independently checked in Go. Build time covers source read/load, frontend analysis/verified MIR, C emission, C compile/link, artifact reads and final EXE write; common warmed toolchain discovery, harness process startup, workspace setup and execution excluded. No persistent package cache; ambient OS caches uncontrolled. No PDB, runtime-speed generalization, Linux, real parser/container workload or cold CLI startup claim.",
